@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] complete-build-inputs
An action's key MUST cover its code, data, declared settings and consumed product identities.
Order-only and reference edges MUST NOT hide reads of derived data. Missing required inputs and
incomplete outputs MUST NOT be treated as a cache hit. Explicit optional files MUST carry a distinct
absent identity when missing, so their appearance, removal and content changes invalidate consumers.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] independent-artifact-ownership
A named product MUST have one owner and a complete byte inventory. Restored outputs MUST be
independent copies; a failed or interrupted restoration MUST NOT leave a successful build stamp.
Native Unreal packages MUST NOT opt into a portable cache until their relocation contract passes.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] advisory-capacity
The capacity planner MUST NOT write scheduler state, grant leases, take locks, launch workloads or
change the live safety system. A queued phase MUST hold no resources or named locks.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] compatible-workspace-incremental-state
Native workspace checkpoints MAY retain and restore existing incremental state across Git revisions
when source fingerprints, complete workspace bytes and engine/SDK compatibility still match. Its
original task/tool provenance MAY be unknown and MUST NOT be invented or promoted into a produced
individual action certificate. Record the receiving observed environment locally; later tool changes
MUST invalidate compatibility-only state. Verified action results MUST retain complete output proof.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] historical-inputs-are-not-capture-head
Historical native source/policy evidence MUST come from the original task's recorded input identities.
A later checkpoint's clean Git revision identifies its capture, not necessarily the producer of every
retained file. Missing historical source evidence MUST cause an ordinary reuse miss; it MUST NOT be
invented from capture HEAD, current source, filenames or the presence of a saved package.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] conservative-native-policy-closure
A supported native geometry policy MUST bind the executed owner/helper closure and current validation
code required by that policy. Unsupported definition-time execution, unresolved local support or
ambiguous historical evidence MUST disable reuse. Historical raw-geometry comparison and current
validator identity MUST remain distinct, so adding a validator cannot silently weaken old geometry proof.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] finalized-reuse-is-the-success-metric
Reported native reuse hits MUST follow successful source/package/current-validator admission and the
successful guarded host finalization for that invocation. Staged candidates, preliminary compatibility
logs and pending unit observations MUST NOT be counted as finalized hits or parent build success.
Refusal diagnostics MUST observe the existing decision without changing admission or receipt identity.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] detached-backup-follows-public-success
Private checkpoint upload scheduling MUST follow verified public release success. Private preparation
before public publication MUST be local only. Spawn, transport or private-publication failure MUST NOT
fail or roll back an already successful public release. Retry MUST preserve the immutable retained
request and completed packs, without requiring recapture or access to the producing checkout.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] frozen-detached-backup-lifetime
A detached backup worker MUST use a digest-checked frozen runtime and cache working directory, with
per-request ownership, bounded transport/deadline and durable failure state. It MUST NOT depend on a
mutable producer checkout or mutable installed module files after detachment. Producer-free resume MUST
verify the durable request's complete destination/source/checkpoint binding and published public readiness.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] pending-publications-protect-shared-packs
Private collection MUST preserve every pack referenced by the newest completed checkpoint or a live
checkpoint/publication pin, including reused packs owned by an older release. A pinned incomplete
publication without a verifiable full reference inventory MUST defer pack deletion. Pin expiry MUST use
the server clock; release tombstones MUST prevent stale clients from resurrecting released pins.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] uncertain-remote-mutations-keep-exclusion
Private pack deletion and metadata consolidation MUST exclude readers and other publishers. A timed-out
or otherwise uncertain remote mutation MUST retain the recovery barrier until its outcome is established;
client exit, local cache presence or an unconfirmed DELETE MUST NOT grant another writer authority.
Deletion MUST remain restricted to the configured private game-cache ownership, never public releases.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] automatic-native-candidates-retain-original-proof
Automatic native retention MUST follow successful guarded host and owning task finalization. It MUST
preserve the original task input evidence and complete validated package groups as immutable candidate
hints, without installing Content or manufacturing receiving/action success. Donor ranking metadata
MUST remain advisory: selection and staging MUST freshly validate the descriptor and byte inventory.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] local-retirement-preserves-useful-successors
Local checkpoint/workspace retirement MUST preserve active work and compatible outputs serving the
current or scheduled builds, including one useful current donor and explicit live pin obligations.
Being referenced by obsolete metadata alone MUST NOT be presented as evidence of ongoing usefulness.
Superseded versions and redundant workspaces MAY retire after scope coverage and current-purpose proof;
an unfinished private restore exercise alone MUST NOT extend a retention hold the operator has retired.
Public release verification and private checkpoint restoration MUST remain separate evidence claims.
Personal backups, shared installed tools and another owner's live outputs MUST remain outside cleanup.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] candidate-composition-keeps-original-groups
Candidate discovery MAY compose independently staged donor catalogues, but MUST preserve each original
task stamp, report and package inventory. A mesh and its collision/LOD source group MUST come from one
compatible donor, never a splice of incomplete histories. Selection MUST compare that donor's original
geometry/owner policy and report, then retain the actual selected donor in per-mesh provenance. Current
loaded import-source and native material/role/collision checks remain mandatory. A corrupt independent
donor MUST miss without hiding another valid donor or creating receiving success.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] local-sweeps-exclude-readers-and-writers
A local metadata publication mutex alone MUST NOT be treated as excluding older unleased readers.
Collection MUST obtain reader/writer exclusion, or an explicitly coordinated quiet boundary covering
every affected old client, without interrupting another owner's native job. It MUST save the retired
metadata and exact deletion inventory outside the collected store, recompute retained references under
exclusion, and refuse changed identities or new references before deleting only authorized obsolete data.
Metadata/blob/workspace removal and observed free-space gain MUST be reported separately: APFS clones
can retain underlying blocks after one pathname is removed. Logical sizes MUST NOT imply physical reclaim.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] owned-material-mesh-imports
A static mesh importer that binds a complete authored material table MUST use the shared
geometry-only Interchange path: no generated placeholder materials/textures and no temporary
mesh rename. Source slot names/order and actual geometry options MUST remain significant.
Current native source, role, material, collision and LOD validation MUST still precede reuse
finalization. Failure to import the exact requested object or retire obsolete owned scratch
packages MUST fail the owner, never publish a successful import report.
